1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:21,679
Bell put the number one on my door in gold. Tank stood beside him with
his arms folded, supervising a nigga with four hands like the fifth
hand was going to be his if that number leaned. He asked whether I
preferred it centered. Nigga, I prefer it accurate. It is your entry
number, Bell said. Tank shook his head.

2
00:00:21,929 --> 00:00:41,161
That's this nigga exit number too. Placements remain to be determined.
Nigga, by who? Bell looked at me. I looked at the gold one. The
professor sighed with the exhaustion of a man who knew engineering
could explain a great many things and none of them would help him win
this conversation.

3
00:00:41,411 --> 00:01:05,262
He nodded as though I had just taught him something about art and
measured the distance from both edges again. The Sundown Circuit
wrapped three times around the academy, crossed a canyon of empty air
between two floating islands, passed through the Crown District, and
ended on the stadium's upper terrace. Twelve drivers had entered.
Every one of them had powers except me.

4
00:01:05,513 --> 00:01:29,453
Their cars glowed, floated, snarled, or did some combination that made
the mechanics back away respectfully. My Lamborghini looked like a
police car had married a bank account and produced a very angry son.
That was enough. Before the race, we met Storm in her private office.
Shawna repeated what Lena had said. Pike showed Finn's release
photograph.

5
00:01:29,703 --> 00:01:51,544
I put the red device from the hall on the dean's desk. She turned it
over and saw the downward wing. The room grew colder. The lower annex
predates my appointment, she said. Voss claims its most sensitive work
is approved by the founding board. He has blocked my access three
times. Then let's make four different, I said.

6
00:01:51,795 --> 00:02:10,115
If I strike at him without securing the school's field, he can put
every person on this island in danger. He already doing that. She met
my eyes. Yes. One honest word. I liked her better for it than all the
titles she had. She knew the circular machine.

7
00:02:10,365 --> 00:02:36,779
Years earlier, before Voss became chancellor, a physicist had proposed
using the Heart to open a passage into a single branch of the past.
The faculty rejected the experiment after a test chamber lost power
and came back coated in frost. The project was supposed to be
dismantled. Dr. Ilya Reiss, its designer, retired soon afterward. Or
got retired underneath us, Tank said.

8
00:02:37,029 --> 00:03:02,298
Storm's hands closed on the arms of her chair. We agreed on two
things. She would keep the academy's main field stable and quietly
move her own trusted people into the control tower. We would get
Sable's case during the race. Nobody would open a time door because
some nigga with a cane had decided ordinary crime lacked imagination.
Shawna listened to every word.

9
00:03:02,548 --> 00:03:23,561
Then she put both palms on the desk. Lena stays in this conversation.
Names on a page won't help her if we forget the woman who got them to
us. Storm nodded. We won't. My wife held her gaze until she believed
it. That was why I loved her. I could fill a room. Shawna could make a
room answer.

10
00:03:23,811 --> 00:03:50,031
By sunset the stadium was packed. Spectators crowded balconies all
along the circuit. Airships hovered outside the lanes, their
passengers leaning over rails with drinks in their hands. A huge
screen showed the drivers as we approached our cars. Victor wore blue
racing leathers. His vehicle was a low silver machine with three
bright rings behind the cockpit. It looked fast standing still.

11
00:03:50,281 --> 00:04:12,978
He caught me admiring it and smiled. Built around my charge pattern.
Nice. It can draw power directly from me. Mine draws power from gas
and disrespect. He laughed. A real laugh this time. Then his face went
serious. Don't leave the marked lane at the canyon. You worried about
me? I'm worried I'll win and you'll have an excuse.

12
00:04:13,228 --> 00:04:37,261
That's friendship trying to happen, nigga. You should stop fighting
it. Across the grid, Shawna kissed me beside the car while every
screen in the stadium showed us. I had one hand at her waist. Her
fingers rested against my neck. The crowd made a sound so loud the
starting official stopped talking. She pulled back smiling. Win
beautifully. You know any other way?

13
00:04:37,511 --> 00:05:00,413
Try coming back without spending another hood. Tank handed me my
helmet. Rosa tied a red ribbon around his wrist for luck, then tied a
blue one around mine because she said two idiots required separate
colors. Tank held his arm away from his body and admired the knot.
Nigga, yours smaller. It's ribbon, Tank. Mine got more future in it.

14
00:05:00,663 --> 00:05:25,568
Rosa caught his wrist before he could compare us under the stadium
lights. Yours is longer because you kept moving. Passion. Fidgeting,
nigga. Victor glanced over from his cockpit. Does the ribbon help?
Tank turned on him with the grave patience of a man encountering
somebody else's tragic childhood. A woman tied it on, nigga. Of course
it helps. I meant aerodynamically.

15
00:05:25,818 --> 00:05:49,635
Now you see why he got one and you don't, Rosa said. Victor opened his
mouth. Closed it. I could almost hear the argument request being
withdrawn inside his head. Shawna reached for the loose end of my
ribbon and tucked it securely beneath the knot. Then she checked the
helmet strap herself. There. Hands free. Chin secure. Ego regrettably
loose.

16
00:05:49,885 --> 00:06:12,992
Baby, that's where the horsepower comes from. Nigga, Bell put a whole
engine behind you. From somewhere under my rear bumper, the professor
said, Thank you. Tank jumped. How long that nigga been under there?
Bell slid out on a low trolley, holding a wrench in one hand and a
timing gauge in another. Long enough to wonder whether affection can
be quantified.

17
00:06:13,242 --> 00:06:37,805
Rosa kissed Tank on the cheek. He went quiet immediately. The
professor looked at him. Apparently. Nigga, finish the car, Tank said,
but he was smiling so hard the warning came out friendly. I lowered
myself into the seat. Shawna rested her hand on the roof and bent
until her face filled the open window. You got everybody? she asked. I
glanced at the mirrors.

18
00:06:38,055 --> 00:07:02,654
My brother. My wife. Rosa beside him. Victor waiting to make me earn
it. Yeah. Then bring them a good race. Nigga, that was the part nobody
put on a timing sheet. Who you wanted waiting when you stopped.
Mercedes and Porsche were already gone. Their part of the race did not
involve driving. Sable would watch from Voss's private terrace above
the Crown District.

19
00:07:02,904 --> 00:07:28,906
She liked expensive company and disliked being bored. Porsche had
spent the afternoon learning both facts from a bartender she tipped
more generously than his employer. Mercedes had secured an invitation
by introducing herself as the woman who knew Captain Aiden before the
sky discovered him. That was technically true, and technically was a
beautiful country. The lights above the grid turned red.

20
00:07:29,156 --> 00:07:53,211
Twelve engines rose. The stadium chanted Victor's name first. He was
theirs. He had earned that. Then my side began. Aiden. Aiden. Aiden.
Both chants crashed together until the whole place sounded like it was
arguing with thunder. Green. We launched. Victor took the lead. A
yellow coupe driven by a woman called Sunfire swept behind him.

21
00:07:53,461 --> 00:08:18,334
I went third, tight against the lane's inner edge. The first turn rose
around the stadium, steep enough to put the sun under my left
shoulder. The Lamborghini gripped. I felt every bit of it: wheel,
road, engine, the gold number on my door announcing the future before
we arrived there. Sunfire's exhaust flashed bright orange. Heat
shimmered over the lane. I couldn't see Victor.

22
00:08:18,584 --> 00:08:42,486
Nigga, I said to nobody, we doing weather already? I waited half a
breath, found the darker line beneath the shimmer, and drove through
it. Her car slid wide. I passed on the inside close enough to see her
turn her head in disbelief. She grinned. Raised two fingers. Then
tried to take her place back. I respected that. The lane dropped
toward the canyon.

23
00:08:42,736 --> 00:09:06,702
For a second the entire city rose above me. The car felt light. My
stomach tried to resign. I held the wheel steady as the tires crossed
onto the narrow field bridge spanning the gap. Victor was a silver
streak ahead. A green car closed behind me, its driver making little
jumps between patches of road. Each jump flashed the air purple.

24
00:09:06,952 --> 00:09:30,400
He appeared on my left, vanished, appeared on my right. Pick a side,
nigga. He appeared ahead of me. I accelerated into the space he had to
leave to make the next jump. When he reappeared, he was behind my rear
bumper. The radio erupted with Bell shouting my name. You anticipated
the recovery interval! Nigga, I anticipated him being annoying!

25
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:50,062
We swept into the Crown District at a speed that made windows reflect
us after we were already gone. High above the road, on Voss's terrace,
Porsche dropped a champagne glass. That was all I saw passing beneath
her. Later she told me the rest. The glass broke near Sable's shoes.

26
00:09:50,312 --> 00:10:09,147
Mercedes caught Porsche by the elbow and apologized with the offended
elegance of a woman whose evening had been spoiled by somebody else's
clumsiness. Sable stood to avoid the spill. Her silver case remained
under her chair. Porsche bent to pick up the largest piece of glass.

27
00:10:09,398 --> 00:10:30,496
Mercedes asked Sable whether Captain Aiden was really as impressive to
the faculty as he had been in Vegas. Sable answered before she
remembered not to. More. That little word cost her the case. Porsche
slid a matching empty case beneath the chair and passed the real one
behind a curtain into Petra's marble hand.

28
00:10:30,746 --> 00:10:55,135
Petra carried it down a service stair while pretending a twelve-pound
locked box was a clutch purse. By the time Sable sat again, Mercedes
had persuaded her to explain why she enjoyed racing. Because it
reveals weakness, Sable said. Mm, Mercedes replied. Depends who
driving. At the end of the first lap, Victor led me by three car
lengths.

29
00:10:55,385 --> 00:11:17,292
At the end of the second, one. He was good. Nigga, he was better than
good. He took the high turns with a precision that made the car look
attached to his thoughts. Blue charge pulsed through the rings behind
him. Whenever I closed, he found another little piece of speed. I
started laughing inside my helmet. Not because he was losing.

30
00:11:17,542 --> 00:11:43,026
Because finally somebody was making me work hard enough to enjoy how
good I was. Then his car screamed. A bright bolt jumped between the
rear rings. The silver body jerked sideways. Victor corrected, but the
rings brightened again, feeding on him. I saw his shoulders stiffen
through the cockpit glass. Victor? Static. Nigga, talk. His voice came
thin through the radio.

31
00:11:43,276 --> 00:12:08,448
The draw won't stop. Bell shouted something to the race officials. The
warning lights along the lane turned amber. Victor's car accelerated.
Not because he wanted it to. The rings pulled harder. Blue light
wrapped his whole body. The silver machine shot toward the canyon at a
speed it could not survive entering the next turn. I followed. Behind
me Sunfire slowed.

32
00:12:08,698 --> 00:12:32,551
The green car vanished toward a safety bay. The spectators' cheers
broke into a different sound. Cut your power, I told Victor. It's
taking it. I heard pain in the last word. Storm's voice entered the
radio. Aiden, I am coming. Can you reach him before the canyon?
Silence for half a second. Enough. I pressed the Lamborghini harder.

33
00:12:32,801 --> 00:12:57,891
Bell's beautiful engine gave me everything it had. The distance
closed. Twenty feet. Ten. Victor's helmet turned toward me. His face
behind the visor looked gray. The man who had wanted to beat me was
disappearing inside his own gift. Don't hit the rings, Bell warned.
They're overloaded. I brought my front bumper level with Victor's rear
wheel. Wasn't planning to.

34
00:12:58,141 --> 00:13:21,137
There was a service split before the canyon, a short lane leading to
an emergency terrace. Victor couldn't turn toward it. His car had
locked itself into a straight hungry line. I could turn him. I struck
the silver car low on its side. The Lamborghini shuddered. Victor's
machine moved six inches. Not enough. Again, he whispered.

35
00:13:21,387 --> 00:13:45,608
Nigga, I would remember that whisper longer than any trophy. I hit him
again. Both cars crossed the split together. The terrace rushed toward
us. My tires shrieked. Victor's rear rings tore bright scars through
the air. We struck the emergency barrier side by side. Foam burst
upward in a white wall. My seat belt tried to cut me in half. Then we
stopped.

36
00:13:45,858 --> 00:14:10,701
For one second all I heard was my own breathing. Then Victor screamed.
I kicked my door open and ran to his car. The cockpit wouldn't
release. Blue light poured through every seam. I caught the handle and
felt heat bite through my glove. Aiden, don't touch the chassis, Bell
shouted. I had already touched it. Electricity snapped up my arm. My
whole body locked.

37
00:14:10,951 --> 00:14:35,555
I fell backward onto the terrace, seeing white. No new power came into
me. No miracle. Just pain and the sharp understanding that a nigga
could absolutely die here. Victor hit the glass from inside. Once.
Weaker the second time. I got up. My left hand shook. I made it hold
the heavy emergency hammer mounted beside the terrace rail. Swung with
the right.

38
00:14:35,805 --> 00:14:57,849
The glass cracked. I swung again. A hole opened. Victor's eyes found
mine. Come on, nigga. I reached through, caught his shoulder strap,
and pulled. He came halfway. The car held the rest of him in its
light. Then a white wind slammed across the terrace. Storm landed
beside me. Her hands spread over the rear rings.

39
00:14:58,099 --> 00:15:20,789
Lightning rose out of them and into her arms. She gasped but held it.
Now. I pulled Victor free. We fell together. The silver car burst
behind us, its rings breaking upward in three bright arcs. Storm bent
the explosion away from the terrace and sent it flowering over empty
sky. The sound rolled around the city.

40
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:45,628
Victor lay against me, breathing in hard little pieces. I took off his
helmet. His eyes opened. Did you win? I looked back at my Lamborghini.
One front corner was buried in foam. The engine was still running.
Hold that thought. Storm stared at me. Captain. He stable? She looked
at Victor, then at the approaching medical team. Yes. I got back in
the car.

41
00:15:45,878 --> 00:16:09,227
Bell made a noise over the radio that might have been a prayer or a
mechanical diagnosis. I put the Lamborghini in reverse. Foam peeled
away from the hood. The wheel pulled left. I held it straight. The
officials were attempting to suspend the race. The other drivers were
already entering the final circuit. Nobody had crossed the line.

42
00:16:09,477 --> 00:16:32,946
The track remained open until they could bring every car safely in. I
rejoined at the service split. In ninth place. Nigga, ninth was
temporary. I passed two cars before the canyon. Three more through the
Crown District. Sunfire saw me in her mirror and laughed so hard I
could see her shoulders move. She gave me no space at all. I found
some anyway.

43
00:16:33,196 --> 00:16:57,447
At the last turn I was second. The green car led. He jumped forward in
a flash of purple. I drove into the space where he needed to finish.
He reappeared beside me. We crossed the line together. The stadium
went silent for one impossible heartbeat. Then the screen showed my
front bumper. Six inches ahead. First. I stopped beneath the finish
arch. Got out.

44
00:16:57,697 --> 00:17:18,606
Took off my helmet. Shawna reached me before anybody else and jumped
into my arms so hard I nearly fell back into the car. You beautiful
fucking lunatic. The whole stadium heard her. The whole stadium
agreed. Tank stood on the hood with both fists up, yelling my name.
Rosa danced beside the car.

45
00:17:18,857 --> 00:17:39,821
Porsche arrived carrying the silver case, and Mercedes kissed it like
a baby she had stolen for a noble cause. Victor came down the medical
ramp leaning on a medic. He stopped in front of me. For a second I
thought he might cry. Instead he took my hand, lifted it over both our
heads, and turned us toward the crowd.

46
00:17:40,071 --> 00:18:01,940
The best driver in the sky, he shouted. That was generous. It was also
geographically cautious. I let him have it. Above us, in his private
box, Voss did not clap. Beside him, Sable opened the empty case. Even
from the track, nigga, I could see the evening leave her face. The
trophy was four feet tall.

47
00:18:02,190 --> 00:18:24,308
They tried handing it to me while Shawna was still in my arms. I
looked at the trophy. Looked at my wife. The official looked at both
and wisely gave the trophy to Tank. This nigga won a building, Tank
said. It's a sculpture, the official told him. Nigga, it got windows.
Decorative panels. Tank turned the thing around.

48
00:18:24,558 --> 00:18:48,737
Somewhere inside it a little gold car circled a track of blue glass.
Aiden, this nigga won a building with a nigga driving inside. I put
Shawna down long enough to admire it. The tiny car crossed a tiny
finish line. Tiny lights flashed. Make sure the little nigga get first
too, I said. The official assured me it was designed that way. Good
design.

49
00:18:48,987 --> 00:19:12,604
Sunfire reached us laughing. Up close she was a brown-skinned woman of
thirty-one with orange curls and a small burn on her racing glove. She
slapped my shoulder, looked at the Lamborghini, and shook her head.
You left the race. Saved that man. Came back and beat all our asses.
Busy evening. No. A busy evening is dinner and a movie.

50
00:19:12,854 --> 00:19:34,299
This nigga took a rescue break from winning. Victor stood beside me,
pale but upright. I was the break. You were the reason, I told him. He
stopped smiling. Only for a second. But the words went somewhere in
him that the trophy didn't reach in me. I'd have done the same, he
said. I know. I did know by then.

51
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:57,683
He had been proud before he met me. Nothing wrong with that. A nigga
with no pride would never have stayed in that broken train's sky long
enough for me to get there. I wasn't interested in shrinking him so I
could look tall. I was already tall enough to make people reconsider
architecture. Bell arrived with all four hands shaking. I need the
car.

52
00:19:57,933 --> 00:20:20,750
You just had the car. I need to understand what you did to it. Tank
pointed at me. This nigga happened to it. Bell touched the hood. The
Lamborghini ticked softly, as if agreeing it had been through an
emotional experience. Then the dean joined us. She embraced Victor
first. He seemed surprised by how tightly she held him.

53
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:40,094
When she let go, she took my unburned hand in both of hers. You
brought him back. He still owed me a fair race. You brought him back,
she repeated. I nodded. That time I let the joke wait. Later, in our
tower, Marcellus opened Sable's case while Tank stood guard at the
door.

54
00:20:40,344 --> 00:21:01,780
It contained paper manifests, a black access seal, and three
photographs held together with a blue ribbon. The first photograph
showed the lower prison. The second showed the circular door. The
third showed a snow-covered station beneath a sky with no floating
islands in it. Men in military coats stood beside a freight wagon.

55
00:21:02,030 --> 00:21:27,320
On the back, in neat black writing, somebody had put a date. February
1944. Shawna turned the photograph over again. Aiden. I see it. Victor
leaned closer. He had stopped being a rival so completely that I
barely noticed when it happened. He was just one more man in the room
whose face hardened because somebody else was being hurt. Marcellus
unfolded a manifest. Names.

56
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:49,771
Ages. Powers where powers existed. Blank spaces where they didn't.
They aren't only taking gifted people, he said. Outside our window,
fireworks celebrated my victory over the clouds. Inside, Shawna
counted the names with her finger, carefully, as if refusing to let a
single one of them disappear between lines.
